From: richard-rhino <richard-rhino@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 04:10:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix positions and KV slots of padded multi-token decode steps

When requests schedule different token counts in one decode step (speculative
decode), the padded tokens of the shorter requests had position 0, so their
keys and values overwrote the slot of the request's first token. They now go to
the pad row.

For models with mrope the same step replaced the 3-axis positions with plain
ones. They are now built per token, flat [3, batch * num_tokens].

Single-token steps are unchanged. Tested on CPU only, not run on HPU.

